  "notes": "TCL 65\" C7L Google TV, 2025, Australia (device G08, model \"Smart TV Pro\", MediaTek tcl9618 / mt5896)\nAndroid 14 (Google TV), firmware UTT2.250416.001 AU02, product G08_4K_GB. About 2.4 GB RAM.\nSame board and firmware build as examples/tcl-c755-google-tv; that list was the starting point, and its\nKeep list holds here unchanged.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/tcl-65c7l-google-tv/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/tcl-65c7l-google-tv/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nADB: Developer options > Wireless debugging was enough; port 5555 answered too, without pairing.\nStock launcher: com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx. Live TV / HDMI app: com.tcl.tv.\nLeft alone: com.tpa.kb (system uid, no running services, purpose unclear) and com.tvos (framework res).\nKept on purpose by this owner: Chromecast, AirPlay, Miracast, Google Assistant (katniss and\ncom.google.android.tv.remote.service, which carries the mic button), the game bar, the USB media\nplayer and gallery, Netflix, Prime Video, YouTube and YouTube Music.\n\nTested 2026-10-22 on a real unit, applied in six batches with screenshots between them: Home, the Input\nbutton's source panel (com.tcl.suspension), Live TV (com.tcl.tv/com.tcl.player.TVActivity), all four\nHDMI inputs in tv_input, YouTube with AdGuard Private DNS, Play Store app updates and every remote button\n(gear, app buttons, Input, mic) kept working with launcherx disabled, so no key helper was enabled. All\n27 packages stayed disabled after a reboot; nothing is re-enabled at boot on this firmware.\n\nKnown quirks on this firmware:\n- The saved Wi-Fi network belonged to setupwraith (dumpsys wifi: cname=...setupwraith). Forget it and\njoin it again in Settings before setupwraith is disabled, or the TV drops off Wi-Fi.\nTCL tracking and analytics",
